From 9d1f15549607d4481df582e6f90d88992d73d47f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 15:31:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] pilotd: on-screen context for Marathon and Android apps

ShowSheetFor maps the process of the window on top to its Keel app
through a desktop entry with Sailjail names. A Marathon app runs as a
marathon-app-runner, which has none, and a pooled runner's command
line does not even name its app. For such a process pilotd asks the
shell (Navigation1.AppIdForPid, which only admitted session services
may call) and uses org.marathonos.<id>, the name the runner serves
Keel Actions under.

An Android app's window belongs to Waydroid's process. For any other
process pilotd asks the shell for the app in front
(Navigation1.GetForegroundApp) and takes it when it is an Android app,
waydroid.<package>: deckardd serves that app's Keel Actions and screen
context under that name. Its name comes from the desktop entry Waydroid
writes for it. Any other process is matched as before.
